+## Bounded peer review: solid-square piece ambiguity
+
+The unchanged production generator at seed 101, default difficulty, sample
+indices 0, 1 and 2 gives three demonstrations without a solid 2x2 code piece.
+The next production draw, sample index 3, contains that texture. The canonical
+decoder turns it right; a rival that turns a solid square left and otherwise
+uses the canonical decoder agrees on all three demonstrations and disagrees on
+the query. Both exact programs and all eight outputs were executed through the
+protected Racket backend. This is a retained findings-only teaching issue, not
+a generator or canonical-rule change, and no frequency claim is made.
+
+The independently usable probe is `workspace/full_square_rival_probe.py`.
+The retained task-local case is in `counterexamples/full-square-rival/`.
+Exact originals remain in `checks/f0f2806877da/full-square-rival/` relative to
+the packet WORK directory, with a command receipt at
+`checks/f0f2806877da/full-square-rival-command.json`. Public challenge bytes are
+separate from private programs and both query answers. A possible repair is to
+replace one demonstration with a solid-square witness while retaining the
+demo count; that repair has not been applied or qualified.
